content.text:
`touch-action` is **not inherited**.

So this:

```css
html, body {
  touch-action: none;
}
```

does not mean every child gets computed `touch-action: none`.

If you need it globally, use:

```css
* {
  touch-action: none;
}
```

or safer/scoped:

```css
app-root,
app-root * {
  touch-action: none;
}
```

But be careful: `touch-action: none` disables browser gestures like scroll, pinch zoom, and swipe behavior. Usually better to apply it only to the actual interactive area that needs custom touch handling, not the whole app.
